                <pb facs="0132" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.24/104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-27T09:00:00-06:00">November 27, 1940—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. My telegram No. 115, November 25, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">2</hi>] p.m.
                    The Foreign Minister has just sent me memorandum referring to our <pb
                        facs="0133" n="121" xml:id="pg121"/> conversation of the 25th and saying
                    that the Guatemalan Government would be pleased to have a United States Army
                    officer sent to Guatemala to make a survey of Guatemalan military needs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
